verview

This experiment explores how chemical treatment (mordanting) and natural dyeing affect the texture, flexibility, and comfort of linen fabrics. Fabrics of the same material can feel different, so I wanted to determine which factors influence tactile properties. By comparing treated vs. untreated linen and repeating tests with hibiscus and onion skin dyes, I isolated the effect of alum treatment and observed its consistent impact on softness and comfort.


Step 1: Preparing the Samples

Four pieces of linen were carefully cut to the same size to ensure consistency. This control allowed fair comparison across all treatments. Maintaining a uniform sample set isa solid foundation for the experiment.
